-- Premium Roblox Simulator SFX: the approved sound set (167 procedural sounds from the "Kick an Egg SFX"
-- workspace), uploaded to Roblox as 8 files to stay far below the monthly audio upload limit:
--   * 3 sound sheets (UI, Gameplay, Sacks): every one-shot is a slice of its sheet, played with PlaybackRegion;
--   * 5 loops as their own files (AvalancheRoll and the premium sacks' idle beds) so they loop seamlessly.
-- SoundBank turns every entry into a SoundBank.CUSTOM replacement. Until a file's id is filled in (and for any
-- event not listed), the built-in recipe plays, so the game never goes silent. Never invent ids: paste the ones
-- Roblox gave the uploads. Keys: SoundBank events, "Sack<tier>.<moment>", "EggLand_<surface>" /
-- "EggBounce_<surface>", "MutationAccent_<mutation>"; several regions = variants (a different one each play).
local PremiumSfx = {}

export type Region = { sheet: string, from: number, to: number }

-- Every file is loudness-matched per tier (routine UI about -20 LUFS ... spectacular -13), so one volume fits all.
PremiumSfx.volume = 0.5
-- Per-event volume tweaks after listening in game (multiplies `volume`), e.g. UIClick = 0.8.
PremiumSfx.gain = {} :: { [string]: number }
-- Transposed per zone like the built-in tone layer (ZoneEnter rises with every zone).
PremiumSfx.tune = { ZoneEnter = true } :: { [string]: boolean }

-- Uploaded asset ids ("rbxassetid://<id>"), "" until uploaded. Files: upload/premium_v1_sheets/KAE_SFX_<sheet>.wav.
PremiumSfx.sheets = {
	UI = "",
	Gameplay = "",
	Sacks = "",
} :: { [string]: string }
-- Files: upload/premium_v1_sheets/KAE_<event>.wav (the dot in Sack events is an underscore in the file name).
